The Security Council,

Expressing its deep concern about the serious humanitarian situation and the deteriorating economic, social, and political conditions in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, which have led to the displacement of millions of Venezuelans across the region,

Expressing concern that the 20 May 2018 presidential elections in Venezuela were neither free nor fair, nor credible, and lacked democratic legitimacy,

Affirming its support for the democratically elected National Assembly of Venezuela as the only legitimate institution representing the will of the Venezuelan people,

Deploring the recent violence and excessive use of force against peaceful and unarmed civilians, and the denial of the entry of vital humanitarian assistance into Venezuela,

Stressing the importance of ensuring the safety and security of all medical and humanitarian personnel, as well as the protection of civilians,

Reaffirming its commitment to the sovereignty, political independence, territorial integrity, and unity of Venezuela, in accordance with the Charter of the United Nations,

1. Expresses its deep concern for the people of Venezuela and the severe shortage of basic goods, including food and medicine;

2. Calls for the immediate start of a peaceful political process leading to free, fair, and credible presidential elections, with international electoral observation, in accordance with Venezuela’s Constitution;

3. Expresses its full support for the National Assembly as the only democratically elected institution in Venezuela, and stresses the need to fully respect the constitutional prerogatives and physical integrity of its members;

4. Urges the immediate and unhindered entry and delivery of humanitarian assistance, in accordance with humanitarian principles, throughout Venezuela to meet the urgent needs of the population;

5. Stresses the necessity of ensuring the safety, freedom of movement, and security of all humanitarian workers and medical personnel providing assistance to civilians;

6. Condemns all acts of violence and the use of force against peaceful demonstrators and calls for restraint by all actors;

7. Requests the Secretary-General to utilize his good offices and coordinate with relevant international and regional partners to facilitate the peaceful transition and delivery of humanitarian assistance, and to report to the Security Council on the implementation of this resolution.

